### [03:07:30 UTC] Step 1 — read_audio/write_audio on synthesized sample
Input: pydub Sine(440) 1s mono mp3 + Sine(440)/Sine(660) 1s stereo mp3, written to scratchpad.
Action: Ran scratchpad/step1_roundtrip.py exercising read_audio() (mono+stereo mp3) and write_audio() (flac mono, wav stereo, unsupported-format branch, pre-normalized data).
Reasoning: Verify bitrate/sample-rate/channels/duration are preserved and that written audio carries real content.
Output: read_audio mono: sr=44100, 44100 samples, ndim=1, ch=1, dur=1000ms, bitrate=63999 (64.0 kbps), dominant freq 440.0 Hz, all finite. Stereo: sr=44100, shape (44100,2), bitrate=127997. write_audio flac: sr=44100, ch=1, dur=1.000s, PCM_24, ~939 kbps effective, dominant freq 440.0 Hz preserved.
  FAILURE: clipped fraction 99.99% (mono flac) and 99.99% (stereo wav). write_audio() passes read_audio()'s raw PCM-scale floats (peak 31212.0) straight to sf.write() with subtype PCM_24, which interprets float input as [-1,1] => everything clamps to full scale. Writing pre-normalized data gives clipped fraction 4.5e-05, confirming the cause is missing scaling in write_audio(), not soundfile.
  write_audio('...mp3') correctly raises ValueError: Unsupported target format: mp3.

